From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerry Zhao <jerryz123@berkeley.edu>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Gate fault-first access-fault generation

RVMODEL_ACCESS_FAULT_ADDRESS is an optional DUT capability. The matching
coverage model already excludes the fault-dependent coverpoint when the macro
is absent, but canonical test generation emits an unconditional LI using the
undefined name. GAS then rejects the symbolic operand in LI's constant-only
implementation.

Guard the generated fault-dependent test chunk with the same capability macro.
DUTs that publish a fault region continue to exercise the coverpoint, while
other DUTs retain valid fault-only-first tests without claiming access-fault
coverage.

---
 .../testgen/src/testgen/coverpoints/vector/cp_custom_vls.py    | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/generators/testgen/src/testgen/coverpoints/vector/cp_custom_vls.py b/generators/testgen/src/testgen/coverpoints/vector/cp_custom_vls.py
index 429dc5e7..46928e60 100644
--- a/generators/testgen/src/testgen/coverpoints/vector/cp_custom_vls.py
+++ b/generators/testgen/src/testgen/coverpoints/vector/cp_custom_vls.py
@@ -121,6 +121,9 @@ def make_cp_custom_ffLS(instr_name: str, instr_type: str, coverpoint: str, test_
         tc.code.insert(0, f"#ifdef {ifdef}")
         tc.code.append("#endif")
 
+    tc.code.insert(0, "#ifdef RVMODEL_ACCESS_FAULT_ADDRESS")
+    tc.code.append("#endif")
+
     tc = test_data.end_test_chunk()
 
     test_data.int_regs.return_register(check_reg)
-- 
